$ apprafter platform autoscale show
[exit 1]
[stdout]
[stderr]
Error: apprafter::cluster::kubectl_failed

  × kubectl get platformstack failed (exit Some(1)): The connection to the
  │ server 127.0.0.1:1 was refused - did you specify the right host or port?
  │ 
  help: The cluster's apiserver did not answer. Check that the target is
        running (`apprafter target ip`), that your kubeconfig points at it
        (`apprafter kubeconfig`), and that nothing between you and port 6443
        is blocking — the origin firewall leaves 6443 open by design, so a
        refusal here is usually a stopped node or a stale kubeconfig.

